The servicing app's ARM adjustment engines, ported for the arm-adjustment
environment's grader.

Source       apps/servicing/src/domain/notices/{arm,arm-verify}.ts
Vendored at  293261b371fe97d2b6b39e1f29ca60dd808ac8fb (apps/servicing/VENDORED_FROM)
Ported       2026-10-21

Each file here is its source byte for byte except its import lines: the
kernel's paths become @hm/kernel/{money,calendar} (the same bytes;
packages/kernel/VENDORED_FROM) and the sibling's .ts becomes .js. Nothing
else may be edited: src/__tests__/arm.test.ts compares each pair with their
import lines removed and fails on any difference. Lint and Prettier skip
this directory for the reason they skip the vendored trees.

arm.ts is engine A (computeArmAdjustment, fixed-scale Decimal) and the pure
helpers around it: the index date and selection, the eighth rounding, the
caps, the payment, the scheduled balance, the (c) and (d) windows and the
send check. arm-verify.ts is engine B (verifyArmAdjustment, BigInt fixed
point), which shares nothing with engine A but the types. The grader runs
both, and a test holds them equal on every generated task.

The service conventions the environment also follows (the schedule row's
dates and notice kind, the expected balance and remaining term, the
interest-only test, which notice goes and how its send date is checked)
live in the servicing app's stateful ops-7-2.ts and ops.ts, which do not
port; they are restated in src/arm/grader.ts with the lines they come from.

To take a change from the servicing app, copy both files again and rewrite
the same six imports.
